#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# color_bar

#% text
# `color_bar` is an option of graphics: `color_bar: [gradient, [lo, hi]]` or `[gradient, [lo, hi], label]` draws a bar of the gradient's colours with a scale from `lo` to `hi` right of the plot.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# In `density_plot` and `contour_plot` the value may be `true`, a bar for the plot's own colours and values, or `false`; `none` draws no bar.

#% item
# The gradient is a name such as `"viridis"`, `"thermal"`, `"cool_warm"` or a list of colours.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
density_plot(sin(x)*cos(y), [x, 0, 3], [y, 0, 3], color_bar: true)
#% output
#= image("color_bar.files/color_bar-1.svgz")

#% cell
contour_plot(x^2 + y^2, [x, -1, 1], [y, -1, 1], color_bar: true)
#% output
#= image("color_bar.files/color_bar-2.svgz")

#% cell
plot(sin(x), [x, 0, 2*pi], color_bar: ["viridis", [0, 1], "level"])
#% output
#= image("color_bar.files/color_bar-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `color_function`, `density_plot`, `contour_plot`, `plot_legends`
